arxiv-2106-12156.description:
A 2021 arXiv research paper by Sindhana Pannir-Sivajothi, Jorge A. Campos-Gonzalez-Angulo, Luis A. Martínez-Martínez, Shubham Sinha, Joel Yuen-Zhou. Supplementary Note 1

We use a generalization of the dark state basis introduced in
strashko2016raman
;
campos2019resonant
to reduce the number of vibrational modes involved in the reaction. The bosonic operator for
\text{D}_{\text{R},c}
, the dark mode highly localized in the
c^{th}
molecule when it is in electronic state
\ket{R}
with total number of reactants
N_{\text{R}}
and products
N_{\text{P}}
is

\displaystyle\hat{a}_{\text{D}}^{(\text{R},c)}=

\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{g_{\text{P}}^{2}N_{\text{P}}+g_{\text{R}}^{2}(N_{\text{R}}-1)}{g_{\text{P}}^{2}N_{\text{P}}+g_{\text{R}}^{2}N_{\text{R}}}}\hat{a}_{\text{R},c}-\frac{g_{\text{R}}^{2}}{\sqrt{g_{\text{P}}^{2}N_{\text{P}}+g_{\text{R}}^{2}N_{\text{R}}}}\frac{1}{\sqrt{g_{\text{P}}^{2}N_{\text{P}}+g_{\text{R}}^{2}(N_{\text{R}}-1)}}\sum_{i\neq c}^{N_{\text{R}}}\hat{a}_{\text{R},i}

(S1)

\displaystyle-\frac{g_{\text{R}}g_{\text{P}}}{\sqrt{g_{\text{P}}^{2}N_{\text{P}}+g_{\text{R}}^{2}N_{\text{R}}}}\frac{1}{\sqrt{g_{\text{P}}^{2}N_{\text{P}}+g_{\text{R}}^{2}(N_{\text{R}}-1)}}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\text{P}}}\hat{a}_{\text{P},j}.
